-- title:
--   The $p$-core $O_p(G)$: the largest normal $p$-subgroup
-- statement:
--   For a prime $p$ and a group $G$, the **$p$-core** $O_p(G)$ is the subgroup generated by all normal subgroups of $G$ that are $p$-groups:
--
--   $$O_p(G)=\Big\langle\, N \;:\; N\trianglelefteq G,\ N \text{ a } p\text{-group}\Big\rangle .$$
--
--   For a finite group the product of two normal $p$-subgroups is a normal $p$-subgroup, so $O_p(G)$ is the largest normal $p$-subgroup of $G$; equivalently it is the intersection of the Sylow $p$-subgroups.
--
--   For a matrix group $H\le\mathrm{GL}(d,p)$, $O_p(H)$ is exactly the kernel of the action of $H$ on the graded space of an invariant composition flag, which is the content of item 1 of Theorem 5.1.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Mathlib has no named $p$-core; it is the supremum of the set of normal subgroups $N$ with `IsPGroup p N`.
-- source:
--   Qiao, Zhang, Testing isomorphism of finite groups in time polynomial in the group order, preprint, Nov. 3, 2026 (held version sha256 eb9a3355…), Theorem 5.1, p.42 (PDF p.46); O_p notation, §3, p.20 (PDF p.24)

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace GroupIsoPoly

namespace Supplement

/-- **The `p`-core `O_p(G)`: the largest normal `p`-subgroup of `G`.**

Qiao, Zhang, *Testing isomorphism of finite groups in time polynomial in the group order*, preprint,
Nov. 3, 2026 (held version sha256 eb9a3355…), Theorem 5.1, p.42 (PDF p.46): "the action of H on the
associated graded space has kernel Op(H)"; notation of §3, p.20 (PDF p.24).

`pCore p G` is the join of all normal subgroups of `G` that are `p`-groups. For a finite group the
product of two normal `p`-subgroups is again a normal `p`-subgroup, so this join is itself the largest
normal `p`-subgroup (equivalently, the intersection of the Sylow `p`-subgroups).

**Formalization Note.** Mathlib has no named `p`-core; this is the join over the set of normal
`p`-subgroups (`IsPGroup p N`), which is the standard definition. -/
def pCore (p : ℕ) (G : Type*) [Group G] : Subgroup G :=
  sSup {N : Subgroup G | N.Normal ∧ IsPGroup p N}

end Supplement

end GroupIsoPoly


